      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given $h(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2x+7}}{\\sqrt{x-7}},$ find $h(10).$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $10$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(10) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2x+7}}{\\sqrt{x-7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2(10)+7}}{\\sqrt{10-7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{27}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{27}{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
