      "problem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt{x-3}$ for $x=15.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $15$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x-3} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{15-3} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify even further using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{12} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 3} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}\\cdot 3} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
