      "problem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt[3]{7r+1}$ at $r=9.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $r$ with $9$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{7r+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{7(9)+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{63+1} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{64} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{4}^{3}} & = \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
